CLASS:: MP3Frames
SUMMARY:: Read a different frame age for every band
CATEGORIES:: UGens>MPEG Audio
RELATED:: Guides/MPEGAudio, Classes/MP3Pack, Classes/MPEGFrame

DESCRIPTION::
Recall complete frames on the stream clock. Scalar ages affect the whole bank. Independent ages combine bands captured at different times.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: ar
The record gate and ages latch at frame start.

ARGUMENT:: fields
An MPEGFrame for the same layer. Encoders, readers and the MPEGFrame constructors all supply this type.

ARGUMENT:: age
One age per band, measured in complete frames. Zero selects live input, one the most recent stored frame. Older ages clamp to available history.

ARGUMENT:: capacity
Fixed history length in complete frames, from 1 to 1024. The default is 64.

ARGUMENT:: record
Set to 0 to stop overwriting history. Live input and recall keep running.

ARGUMENT:: clear
A rising edge discards history at the next frame boundary.

ARGUMENT:: downsample
Native clock divisor from 1 to 6. A reader samples this at start. Connected field streams preserve the original codec clock.

RETURNS:: An MPEGFrame containing the recalled fields and the live timing marker.

EXAMPLES::
code::
{ var f = MPEGFrame.mp3(SinOsc.ar([2,3,5])*12, gain:171); var m = MP3Frames.ar(f,(0..31)%4,8); Limiter.ar(MP3Decode.ar(m),0.15) ! 2 }.play;
::
